      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Detecting advanced backend data processing within a proprietary application or firmware is extremely difficult for the average user. Reverse engineering the app or firmware would typically require highly specialized technical skills, as the most sensitive processing usually occurs on secured servers, not on your phone or shoe itself. Privacy advocates often suggest using privacy-focused services or side-loading apps that audit permissions, but full certainty is elusive.",
